<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16991" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτέκμαρτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>without distinctive mark,
				obscure, baffling,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρηστήριον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					5.92
				</span></i>
			.
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γ́; μοῖρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					910
				</span></i>
			 (
				Sup.
			); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρημία</span>”
				<i>trackless,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Luc.</u>
					14
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτέκμαρτον προνοῆσαι</span>
			<i>without mark</i> whereby to judge it, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				10.63
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. δέος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					4.63
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				638a
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως, ἔχειν ὅτου ἕνεκά ἐστι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Mem.</u>
					1.4.4
				</span></i>
			: neut. pl. as Adv., <i>bafflingly,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				7.45
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of persons,
				<i>uncertain, inconsistent,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				170
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>boundless, unlimited,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδωρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Orph.
					<u>A.</u>
					1150
				</span></i>
			: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γαστήρ</span> dub. in
				<i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				2.206
			</span></i>.</div>
